The full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
A human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The code in this repository — `demos/`, `tools/`, `site/` and everything
outside `docs/` — is MIT instead; see the `LICENSE` file at the root. The split
is deliberate: a lecturer should be able to take an example demo into a course
without a licence question, and the documents should be quotable with
attribution.
